From ec7cf364bd410ee814a60549b41f87fa5b8e82c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mingyang Sun (Public)" <Mingyang.Sun@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:12:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/16] fix(clr): gate only the block16 converts, not the whole
 gfx1250 OCP path

The previous commit disabled HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_OCP_BUILTINS entirely for
gfx1250-strict. That is too coarse: the macro also gates conversions that
gfx1250-strict does support, so those fell back to software unnecessarily.
Measured on gfx1250-strict:

  __amd_cvt_fp8_to_float   v_cvt_f32_fp8_e32, 10 instrs -> 62 instrs (software)
  FP8 convert loop         9.86 ms -> 74.06 ms  (7.5x slower)

For reference the same loop takes 9.44 ms on the pre-split gfx1250 path, so
the previous commit regressed against the behaviour it was meant to restore.
The gfx1250 FP4/FP6 pack helpers in amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp were affected the same
way.

Only the block16 unpack ops are missing on gfx1250-strict. Introduce a
separate HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_BLOCK16_BUILTINS predicate, restore
HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_OCP_BUILTINS to its previous definition, and require the
new predicate on exactly the 30 preprocessor blocks that reference a block16
unpack builtin (8 in amd_hip_fp4.h, 12 in amd_hip_fp6.h, 10 in
amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp). Everything else keeps using hardware on gfx1250-strict.

Verified mechanically that no block referencing a block16 builtin is left
ungated, and that no block gated by the new predicate uses only builtins that
are still available.

Behaviour now matches the pre-split path, which emulated only the ops the
target lacks. Compared bit-exactly against it across 9664 conversions --
every FP4 code, every FP6 E2M3/E3M2 code, every FP8 E4M3/E5M2 code, the
__amd_cvt_* family, and 512-point forward sweeps from float, double and half
through FP4/FP6/FP8 including x2 pack/unpack:

  this change          3 mismatches / 9664
  without the fix   1941 mismatches / 9664

The 3 remaining mismatches are the negative-zero code converting to half
(fp4 code 8, fp6 code 32), which returns 32768.0 instead of -0.0. That is a
pre-existing defect in the shared fcbx software path, reproducible on the
host with unmodified headers, and is tracked separately.

Other measurements on gfx1250-strict:

  fp4 roundtrip   9/10 mismatches -> 0/10
  fp6 roundtrip   7/8  mismatches -> 0/8
  fp8             v_cvt_f32_fp8_e32 / v_cvt_pk_fp8_f32, unchanged
  fp4 pack        v_cvt_scalef32_pk8_fp4_f32, still hardware
  gfx1250         unchanged

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 8778233019ad56e1d4d2116f9b45f78e1ff55392)
